  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Building Capacity for M&amp;E of Social Development Impacts in Tourism Sector</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The goal of the grant is to assist the newly-created Ministry of Tourism (MT) in planning, managing, and implementing sustainable tourism development by promoting and consolidating an effective results-based monitoring and evaluation system (M&amp;E.).  This system will build on the existing M&amp;E framework in the MT and help to strengthen linkages with associated regulatory/safeguard ministries, such as the Ministry of Cities and the Ministry of Environment, related to tourism planning and development. The grant will support tourism planning and M&amp;E capacity at the federal and state level and conduct pilot planning, and building of performance and results indicators in two unique tourism circuits, currently being designed: (a) the Estrada Real, a historical and environmental circuit in the Minas Gerais state, that dates from the 17th Century, cutting across one of the poorest rural areas of the state; and (b) a unique cultural circuit in the Bahia state, with strong Afro-descendent elements.</narrative>
  </description>
